1 mark: A = {5, 10, 15, 20}, B = {3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18}
1 mark: C = {1, 2, 4, 5, 10, 20}
2 marks: (a) A n B = {15}, probability = 1/20
2 marks: (b) A U B has 9 elements, probability = 9/20
2 marks: (c) A n B n C = { } (empty), probability = 0

1 mark: (a) M = {(4, 6), (5, 5), (6, 4)}
2 marks: (a) N = {(1, 4), (2, 5), (3, 6), (4, 1), (5, 2), (6, 3)}
1 mark: (b) P(M) = 3/36 = 1/12 and P(N) = 6/36 = 1/6
2 marks: (b) P(M or N) = 1/12 + 1/6 = 1/4
2 marks: (c) yes, M and N are mutually exclusive since they have no element in common (n(M n N) = 0)

1 mark: (a) gradient = (-3 - (-3))/(1 - 2) = 0
2 marks: (a) equation of the line: y = -3
3 marks: (b)(i) correct multiplication table modulo 7 on {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}
2 marks: (b)(ii) I. commutative, because the table is symmetric about the leading diagonal (a (x) b = b (x) a)
2 marks: (b)(ii) II. 4 (x) 6 = 3, 5 (x) 4 = 6, 3 (x) 6 = 4
2 marks: (b)(ii) III. n^2 = n (mod 7): truth set {0, 1}
